`lib/Pod/Weaver/PluginBundle/Author/GETTY.pm:183-185` writes, whenever a bugtracker URL is known:

    Please report bugs and feature requests on GitHub at L<$bugtracker_web>.

Since the bundle got `Author::GETTY::GiteaMeta`, `bugtracker.web` is also set for Gitea/Forgejo/Codeberg dists (`GiteaMeta.pm:174`), so their woven POD reads "on GitHub at https://codeberg.org/...". Affected today: p5-www-gitea (origin `git@codeberg.org:getty/p5-www-gitea.git`), and every dist that moves to src.ci.

Done when the sentence does not name a forge it cannot know (drop "on GitHub", or derive the name from the URL host), with a test next to the existing weaver/GiteaMeta tests.

